          "title": "You'll want to know: چولہا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چولہا — chūlhā — \"a stove\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چولہا (chūlhā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cullī, \"fireplace\" (CDIAL 4879). CDIAL takes the Sanskrit word from Dravidian."
            }
          ]
        },
